---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How this site handles enquiry data, technical records and future analytics choices."
  path="/privacy/"
  updated="24 Aug 2026"
>
  <h2>Scope of this notice</h2>
  <p>
    This notice covers the public Data Decision Consulting website and its diagnostic enquiry form.
    Client project data is handled under the terms agreed for that engagement.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you choose to provide</h2>
  <p>
    The enquiry form asks for your work email, company or website, a short description of what you
    want to understand, optional notes about the analytics and CRM systems you use today, the
    service your enquiry relates to where applicable, and consent to a response. Hidden fields may
    capture campaign parameters and the referring page so the enquiry source can be understood.
  </p>
  <p>
    The form uses automated-spam checks, including a hidden field and a minimum completion time.
  </p>

  <h2>Form delivery</h2>
  <p>
    When you submit the enquiry form, the entered information and ordinary request metadata are
    processed by a form-delivery service and forwarded to Data Decision Consulting by email. You can
    email Data Decision Consulting directly instead of using the form.
  </p>

  <h2>Purposes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Review and respond to a requested diagnostic or partnership enquiry.</li><li>
      Assess fit and prepare a written scope.
    </li><li>Protect the form and diagnose delivery failures.</li><li>
      Understand aggregate enquiry sources after an approved analytics setup exists.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Retention and recipients</h2>
  <p>
    The form-delivery service processes the submission so it can reach Data Decision Consulting.
    Data Decision Consulting keeps the resulting enquiry record only as long as needed to respond,
    assess fit, meet applicable obligations and maintain necessary business records.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site currently uses no third-party analytics or non-essential cookies. Interaction events
    used by the interface remain in the page and are not sent to an analytics service. See the <a
      href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    To ask about information supplied through this site, email <a
      href="mailto:contact@datadecision.consulting">contact@datadecision.consulting</a
    >. You may ask Data Decision Consulting to correct or delete enquiry information, subject to any
    record that must be retained for an applicable obligation.
  </p>

  <h2>Security and limits</h2>
  <p>
    Data Decision Consulting limits the information requested and uses a specialist delivery service
    for the enquiry form. No website or email workflow can promise absolute security.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
